{"step_index":253,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:43:11Z","input_tokens":2637,"cache_read_tokens":96816,"output_tokens":587,"content":"**Spotify: Keep Flatpak.**\n* Running Debian Sid (`forky`). Official Spotify `.deb` targets old Ubuntu LTS — breaks often on rolling library updates (OpenSSL/FFmpeg).\n* Flatpak bundles dependencies/codecs, auto-updates cleanly via Flathub, no system breakage.\n* *(Only keep Native if modding with Spicetify).*\n\n**Steam: Keep Native (APT).**\n* Direct GPU driver access, easier secondary storage/drives, native GameMode / MangoHud / controller support.\n* Flatpak Steam needs sandbox overrides (`flatpak override`) for extra disk paths and system tooling.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended cleanup commands\n\n**1. Remove duplicate Native Spotify (keep Flatpak):**\n```sh\nsudo apt purge spotify-client\nsudo rm -f /usr/local/share/applications/spotify.desktop\n```\n\n**2. Remove duplicate Flatpak Steam (keep Native):**\n```sh\nflatpak uninstall com.valvesoftware.Steam\n```","thinking":"Initial observation: user lacks a Spicetify installation. The operating system is Debian testing/unstable. Spotify's APT package is prone to breakage on this distribution due to dependency conflicts. The Flatpak version offers a robust solution due to its isolated runtime and bundled codecs, which avoid these conflicts.\n\n\n"}
